      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Common indicators of neighborhood renewal include rising commercial rents, increased property values, and a demographic shift toward higher-income, often younger, professional residents. Economic improvement is frequently marked by the arrival of small boutique retailers and cafes alongside the decline of budget establishments like dollar stores. Additionally, you might observe physical transformations such as new construction, facade renovations, and a surge in public safety or municipal investment. These socio-economic changes collectively signal the transition from disinvestment to what sociologists term \"gentrification,\" which can significantly alter the social fabric of the area.",
