    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. It sounds like the \"new\" crowd brings more investment, but the \"old\" crowd just gets pushed out. When you're looking at these neighborhood studies, how do researchers usually describe the quality of life or the \"vibe\" of the community as it changes? Like, is there a difference in how the two groups are characterized in academic literature regarding their contribution to the area's stability or culture?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
